{"name":"Think Pink","hex":"#e5a5c1","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"think","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To ponder, to go over in one's mind.","To have (some statement) in one's mind; to say to oneself mentally."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An act of thinking; consideration (of something)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/think"},{"term":"pink","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A color reminiscent of pinks, the flowers.","Magenta, the colour evoked by red and blue light when combined."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a colour between red and white; pale red.","Of a fox-hunter's jacket: scarlet."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pink"}],"entries":[{"title":"Think Pink","blocks":[{"text":"Think Pink is the debut album by English psychedelic musician Twink. Recorded in 1969, the album was released on Sire Records in the US in 1970 and Polydor Records in the UK in early 1971. It was produced by Mick Farren and featured members of The Pretty Things, The Deviants, plus Steve Peregrin Took of Tyrannosaurus Rex. The final two tracks were the only commercial release of any songs written by Took until 1990, ten years after his death."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/c/c3/Twink_-_Think_Pink_album_cover.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Think_Pink","wikidata":"Q7784523"},{"title":"Think Pink (clothing)","blocks":[{"text":"Think Pink is an Italian sportswear brand offering clothes and accessories, for men, women, and children founded in the late 1970s and come to success in the early eighties. Previously owned by the Tecnica Group., is now a trademark belonging to Man Socks Italia S.r.l."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/2/22/THINK_PINK_logo.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Think_Pink_(clothing)","wikidata":"Q7784524"},{"title":"Pink","blocks":[{"text":"Pink is a pale tint of red or rose, the color of the pink flower. It was first used as a color name in the late 17th century. A combination of pink and white is associated with innocence, whereas a combination of pink and black links to eroticism and seduction."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg/330px-Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pink","wikidata":"Q429220"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/c/c3/Twink_-_Think_Pink_album_cover.png/250px-Twink_-_Think_Pink_album_cover.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/c/c3/Twink_-_Think_Pink_album_cover.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/c/c3/Twink_-_Think_Pink_album_cover.png/250px-Twink_-_Think_Pink_album_cover.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATwink_-_Think_Pink_album_cover.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg/500px-Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg/500px-Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APink_sapphire_ring.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/Burano_Hausfassade_W%C3%A4sche-20090315-RM-113043.jpg/500px-Burano_Hausfassade_W%C3%A4sche-20090315-RM-113043.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumb